\section*{Invariant anticanonical sections with nonzero Euler characteristic}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
Invariant sections in unbounded anticanonical degrees with a fixed negative pseudo-effective error are claimed to produce a positive-degree untwisted invariant section, yielding smooth semipositive anticanonical nonvanishing. The cited manuscript argues for that result; its relation to this problem is specified below.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Manuscript 1 (family 068, 2026-09-26): Character-sensitive transfer chooses a base from invariant section systems and tracks exact direct-image lines. In the separate harmonic construction, approximation of the pulled-back base metric forces base canonical covectors into a weak-limit representative, making restriction to a general fiber detect its class; compact-monodromy descent then returns sections to the original variety.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
Manuscript 1 (family 068, 2026-09-26): The problem selects the mathematical statement summarized here, including its stated hypotheses and parameter range. The cited theorem gives a claimed proof of that assertion in full.

\subsection{Formal verification}
